      "problem": "Normalize the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
